{#
    The shared look of a purchase status and an amount (NFR-094, NFR-X05).

    Included inside the `<style>` block of both shells that render purchases, so the parent's
    screen and the child's agree about what "Pending" looks like without either owning the other's
    stylesheet.

    **Nothing here carries meaning by colour alone.** Every status is rendered as its own word —
    "Pending parent approval", "Confirmed", "Denied" — and the border and background only
    reinforce it. Remove all of this and the pages still say exactly the same things, which is the
    test NFR-094 asks a colour to pass.
#}
.status { display: inline-block; padding: .15rem .5rem; border-radius: .25rem; border: 1px solid currentColor; font-weight: 600; }
.status-pending { color: #92400e; background: #fffbeb; }
.status-approved, .status-not_required { color: #14532d; background: #f0fdf4; }
.status-denied { color: #7f1d1d; background: #fef2f2; }
.status-expired { color: #3f3f46; background: #fafafa; }

/* The amount is the number a parent is being asked about, so it is never the smallest thing on
   the card. */
.amount { font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; white-space: nowrap; }

.purchase-card { border: 1px solid #d4d4d4; border-left-width: .35rem; border-radius: .5rem; padding: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
.purchase-card h3 { margin: 0 0 .25rem; }
.purchase-card .meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .25rem 1.25rem; margin: .5rem 0; }
.purchase-card .notes { border-left: 3px solid #d4d4d4; padding-left: .75rem; margin: .5rem 0 0; }

/* NFR-X05: at 320px the card's header stacks, and the amount stays visible because it is a
   sibling of the title rather than something in a column that scrolled away. */
.purchase-card .headline { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .5rem 1rem; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }

.badge { display: inline-block; min-width: 1.5rem; padding: 0 .4rem; border-radius: .75rem; background: var(--brand, #1f2937); color: #fff; text-align: center; font-weight: 700; }
